## Summary

**Bug**: When GNSS is stopped, the filter text ("Showing X of Y satellites") remains visible on screen instead of being cleared.

**Root cause**: The `gpsStop()` method in `GpsStatusFragment.java` (line 448) was empty — it performed no action when GNSS was stopped. The filter group (`filterGroup`) and its text (`filterTextView`) were never updated when the GPS turned off.

**Fix**: Added two lines to `GpsStatusFragment.gpsStop()`:
1. `PreferenceUtils.saveGnssFilter(new LinkedHashSet<GnssType>())` — clears the saved GNSS filter preference (empty set = "show all")
2. `updateFilterView()` — re-evaluates the filter state and hides the filter group (sets `View.GONE`) since the filter is now empty

This ensures the filter text disappears when GNSS stops, matching the expected behavior described in the bug report.

